1
00:00:03,109 --> 00:00:05,349
The same tree has blossoms in spring,

2
00:00:05,399 --> 00:00:07,391
leaves in summer, snow in winter…

3
00:00:07,441 --> 00:00:09,731
Why do the seasons change every year?

4
00:00:10,528 --> 00:00:12,221
Noah thinks Earth gets closer

5
00:00:12,271 --> 00:00:13,483
to the Sun in summer.

6
00:00:13,533 --> 00:00:15,106
But Mila takes out a globe…

7
00:00:15,156 --> 00:00:15,827
it's tilted!

8
00:00:15,877 --> 00:00:16,779
That's the key.

9
00:00:17,572 --> 00:00:19,086
Discovery mission!

10
00:00:21,602 --> 00:00:22,059
Mini mode!

11
00:00:22,109 --> 00:00:23,988
Earth goes around the Sun in one year,

12
00:00:24,038 --> 00:00:26,830
and its axis stays tilted, always in the same direction.

13
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:29,063
So sometimes the North leans toward the Sun,

14
00:00:29,113 --> 00:00:30,737
sometimes it leans away from it.

15
00:00:31,530 --> 00:00:34,730
Leaning toward the Sun, the North gets the rays head-on,

16
00:00:34,780 --> 00:00:37,167
so it heats up strongly and days are long…

17
00:00:37,217 --> 00:00:37,864
it's summer!

18
00:00:37,914 --> 00:00:40,533
But leaning away, it gets the rays at a slant,

19
00:00:40,583 --> 00:00:41,636
and days are short…

20
00:00:41,686 --> 00:00:42,382
it's winter.

21
00:00:43,188 --> 00:00:46,744
During the North's summer, the South leans the other way,

22
00:00:46,794 --> 00:00:48,452
so down there, it's winter!

23
00:00:48,502 --> 00:00:50,526
And six months later, they swap.

24
00:00:51,311 --> 00:00:52,555
And what about distance?

25
00:00:52,605 --> 00:00:55,843
In fact, Earth is even a little closer to the Sun in January,

26
00:00:55,893 --> 00:00:57,352
in the middle of our winter!

27
00:00:57,402 --> 00:00:58,857
So distance hardly matters.

28
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:01,602
And that's why the seasons change.

29
00:01:03,199 --> 00:01:06,265
Earth is tilted: the half tilted toward the Sun has summer,

30
00:01:06,315 --> 00:01:07,688
the other half has winter.

31
00:01:08,685 --> 00:01:11,910
With an adult: shine a flashlight on a sheet of paper,

32
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:13,729
straight on, then at an angle.

33
00:01:13,779 --> 00:01:16,337
At an angle, the spot is bigger and weaker…

34
00:01:16,387 --> 00:01:17,114
like winter!

35
00:01:17,881 --> 00:01:19,631
And why is the sea salty?

36
00:01:19,681 --> 00:01:21,121
The answer tomorrow.
